## 6. Features

- Browse, search, and filter movies by title, genre, language, and city
- Showtimes grouped by date, theater, and time with live seat-availability coloring
- 12×12 interactive seat map (144 seats/screen)
- **Real payment processing via Razorpay** (UPI, cards, netbanking, wallets — all handled by Razorpay's own secure checkout, no card data touches this app's servers)
- Pay-at-theater (cash) option for offline payment
- Booking confirmation screen with a downloadable PDF ticket
- Automatic booking confirmation by email, with optional SMS
- "My Bookings" page: view, download ticket, and cancel any booking
- **Admin: Manage Theaters** — add new theaters, screens, and seat counts
- **Admin: Manage Posters** — correct a movie's poster by pasting an image URL
- JWT-based login/register

## 7. Admin Guide

### Creating the demo accounts

Admin status is stored on the user (`role: "admin"`) and is never granted by registration. The demo accounts are created by a script:

```bash
cd server
npx tsx scripts/seedDemoUsers.ts
```

It creates (or repairs) `demo@moviebook.com` and `admin@moviebook.com` using the database in `MONGODB_URI`, so if the deployed backend uses the same database the accounts work on the live site too. To make any other registered user an admin, run `npx tsx scripts/makeAdmin.ts their@email.com`.

### Managing theaters

Log in as the admin. A **Theaters** link appears in the top bar (it is hidden for normal users); it opens `/admin/theaters`, where you can:
- Add a theater: name, city/location, address, number of screens, seats per screen.
- Tick "create showtimes" (on by default) so the new theater gets showtimes for the next 7 days for the top-rated movies. The city filter and movie pages are built from showtimes, so this is what makes a new theater show up on the site.
- Delete a theater. A theater that already has showtimes cannot be deleted.

### Managing posters

Go to `/admin/posters`. Paste a correct image URL (e.g. copied from Wikipedia or TMDB) for any movie and save — updates instantly.

## 8. Payment Flow (Razorpay)

1. User selects seats and proceeds to checkout.
2. A booking is created on the backend with `paymentStatus: "PENDING"`.
3. The backend creates a Razorpay order (`POST /api/payments/create-order`) for the booking's total amount.
4. Razorpay's Checkout.js modal opens in the browser, where the user completes payment by any method Razorpay supports.
5. On success, Razorpay returns a payment ID, order ID, and signature to the frontend.
6. The frontend sends these to the backend (`POST /api/payments/verify`), which **re-computes the signature server-side** using the Razorpay secret key and compares it — this is what proves the payment is genuine and wasn't forged client-side.
7. If verification succeeds, the booking's `paymentStatus` is updated to `"PAID"` and the confirmation screen is shown.

### Testing payments (Razorpay test mode)

With `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`/`RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` set to **test mode** keys (starting with `rzp_test_`), use Razorpay's published test card to complete a payment without real money:
```
Card number: 4111 1111 1111 1111
Expiry:      any future date
CVV:         any 3 digits
```
For UPI testing in test mode, Razorpay's checkout simulates success automatically for any UPI ID ending in `@razorpay`.

## 9. Database Schema (collections)

| Collection | Key fields |
|---|---|
| `users` | name, email, password (hashed), phone, role (`user` or `admin`) |
| `movies` | title, description, genre[], language, releaseDate, duration, poster, rating |
| `theaters` | name, location, address, screens: [{ name, totalSeats }] |
| `showtimes` | movie, theater, screen, showDate, startTime, endTime, price, totalSeats, availableSeats, bookingSeats[] |
| `seats` | showtime, seatNumber, row, seatType, price, status |
| `bookings` | user, showtime, seats[], totalAmount, bookingStatus, paymentStatus, bookingNumber, razorpayOrderId, razorpayPaymentId |

## 10. API Reference

See `server/README.md` for the full endpoint table. New endpoints added for this update:

| Route | Method | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/admin/check` | GET | ✓ Admin | Confirms the logged-in user is an admin |
| `/admin/theaters` | GET | ✓ Admin | List theaters |
| `/admin/theaters` | POST | ✓ Admin | Create a theater (optionally with showtimes) |
| `/admin/theaters/:id` | PUT | ✓ Admin | Update a theater |
| `/admin/theaters/:id` | DELETE | ✓ Admin | Delete a theater (blocked if it has showtimes) |
| `/admin/movies/:id/poster` | PATCH | ✓ Admin | Update a movie's poster URL |
| `/seat-locks` | POST | ✓ | Lock seats for 10 minutes before online payment |
| `/payments/create-order` | POST | ✓ | Create a Razorpay order for a booking |
| `/payments/verify` | POST | ✓ | Verify a completed Razorpay payment |

